#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:79
msgid "Similarities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:81
msgid ""
"This function is _similar_ to the intrinsic function `encodeURI`. "
"However, it will not encode:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:83
msgid "The `\\`, `^`, or `|` characters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:84
msgid "The `%` character when it's part of a valid sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:85
msgid "`[` and `]` (for IPv6 hostnames)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:86
msgid ""
"Replaces raw, unpaired surrogate pairs with the Unicode replacement "
"character"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:88
msgid ""
"As a result, the encoding aligns closely with the behavior in the [WHATWG"
" URL specification][whatwg-url]. However, this package only encodes "
"strings and does not do any URL parsing or formatting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/encodeurl_README.md:90
msgid ""
"It is expected that any output from `new URL(url)` will not change when "
"used with this package, as the output has already been encoded. "
"Additionally, if we were to encode before `new URL(url)`, we do not "
"expect the before and after encoded formats to be parsed any differently."
msgstr ""

